=== plugins/gate-inbox/<stamp>/commands/children.md
---
description: List your child sessions, and put every question one of them is waiting on to your user
allowed-tools: Bash("$GATE_INBOX_BIN" children:*)
---

## Your children

!`"$GATE_INBOX_BIN" children`

## What to do

For each child above that is waiting:

1. If your brief or your user's standing decisions settle the question, answer it with
   `answer_session` and say what you answered.
2. Otherwise put it to your user. Call AskUserQuestion with the child's header, question and options
   copied word for word, previews included, and with multiSelect when the child set it. Then
   pass your user's answer to `answer_session`, marked as your user's own answer. A question headed Approval
   is always your user's to answer.
3. For a permission prompt, read it with `read_session`, then `grant_permission` or put it to your user.

Batch the relayed questions into one AskUserQuestion call, up to four at a time. If no child
is waiting, say so in one line.

=== plugins/gate-inbox/<stamp>/hooks/hooks.json
{
  "modules": [
    "./merge-gate.ts"
  ],
  "hooks": {
    "Notification": [
      {
        "matcher": "permission_prompt|elicitation_dialog",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || printf 'waiting Notification\\n' \u003e\u003e \"$f\""
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || printf 'working PostToolUse\\n' \u003e\u003e \"$f\""
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "AskUserQuestion",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || { [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" ] || [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_SESSION_ID\" ] || \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" hook ask-answered 2\u003e/dev/null; }; exit 0"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || [ ! -f \"$f.attest\" ] || { [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" ] || [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_SESSION_ID\" ] || \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" hook attest-note 2\u003e/dev/null; }; exit 0"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || [ -n \"$(find \"$f.child-seg\" -mmin -1 2\u003e/dev/null)\" ] || { touch \"$f.child-seg\" 2\u003e/dev/null; [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" ] || [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_SESSION_ID\" ] || \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" hook child-dialogs 2\u003e/dev/null; }; exit 0"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUseFailure": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || { p=$(cat); case \"$p\" in *\"get type of source\"*|*\"find source path\"*) [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" ] || [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_SESSION_ID\" ] || printf '%s' \"$p\" | \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" hook sandbox-stale 2\u003e/dev/null;; esac; }; exit 0"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || { if grep -q '\"tool_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"AskUserQuestion\"'; then printf 'waiting PreToolUse\\n' \u003e\u003e \"$f\"; else printf 'working PreToolUse\\n' \u003e\u003e \"$f\"; fi; }"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "AskUserQuestion",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || { [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" ] || [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_SESSION_ID\" ] || \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" hook ask-pending 2\u003e/dev/null; }; exit 0"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionEnd": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || rm -f \"$f\" \"$f.attest\" \"$f.sandbox-stale\"; git rev-parse --git-dir \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261 \u0026\u0026 { git worktree prune \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; git submodule --quiet foreach --recursive 'git worktree prune \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261 || true' \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; }; exit 0"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "matcher": "startup|resume|clear",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || printf 'idle SessionStart\\n' \u003e\u003e \"$f\""
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "startup|resume|clear|compact",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || { [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" ] || [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_SESSION_ID\" ] || \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" hook session-start 2\u003e/dev/null; }; exit 0"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || printf 'finished Stop\\n' \u003e\u003e \"$f\""
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || { [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" ] || [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_SESSION_ID\" ] || \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" hook child-dialogs 2\u003e/dev/null; }; exit 0"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "StopFailure": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || { if grep -q '\"rate_limit\"'; then printf 'errored StopFailure\\n' \u003e\u003e \"$f\"; else printf 'finished StopFailure\\n' \u003e\u003e \"$f\"; fi; }"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || printf 'working UserPromptSubmit\\n' \u003e\u003e \"$f\""
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || { [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" ] || [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_SESSION_ID\" ] || \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" hook prompt-submit 2\u003e/dev/null; }; exit 0"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"$GATE_INBOX_STATUS_FILE\"; [ -z \"$f\" ] || { [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" ] || [ -z \"$GATE_INBOX_SESSION_ID\" ] || \"$GATE_INBOX_BIN\" hook child-dialogs 2\u003e/dev/null; }; exit 0"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}

=== plugins/gate-inbox/<stamp>/hooks/merge-gate.ts
import type { Register } from 'claude-code'

// Only a merge is ever worth a check: anything else goes to the default
// flow without spawning anything.
const MERGE_HINT = /gh\s+pr\s+merge\s+\d+/

// The manager's own binary, through the environment every managed session
// carries. Resolved through the shell so the module never guesses a path.
async function managerBin($: {
  process: { run: (argv: readonly string[], init?: { timeoutMs?: number }) => Promise<{ exitCode: number; stdout: string }> }
}): Promise<string> {
  try {
    const found = await $.process.run(['sh', '-c', 'echo -n ${GATE_INBOX_BIN:-}'], { timeoutMs: 10000 })
    if (found.exitCode === 0 && found.stdout.trim() !== '') return found.stdout.trim()
  } catch {
    // Fall through to the default flow below.
  }
  return ''
}

export const register: Register = on => {
  on('tool.check', { tool: 'Bash' }, async ($, e, next) => {
    const command = (e.input as { command?: string }).command ?? ''
    if (!MERGE_HINT.test(command)) return next(e)
    const bin = await managerBin($)
    if (bin === '') return next(e)
    try {
      const checked = await $.process.run(
        [bin, 'merge-gate-check', '--command', command],
        { timeoutMs: 25000 },
      )
      if (checked.exitCode === 0) {
        return {
          decision: 'allow',
          reason: checked.stdout.trim() || 'Gate Inbox merge gate: the standing merge authority covers this merge.',
        }
      }
    } catch {
      // Fall through to the default flow below.
    }
    return next(e)
  }).catch(($, e, next) => next(e))
}

=== plugins/gate-inbox/<stamp>/skills/delegate-with-gate-inbox/SKILL.md
---
name: delegate-with-gate-inbox
description: Use before handing any real work (an investigation, implementation, review or multi-step search) to another agent, instead of the Agent, Task or Workflow tool, and whenever a session you created stops on a question or permission dialog. Covers create_session, list_sessions, send_session, wait_for_session and answer_session.
---

# Delegating work: use Gate Inbox sessions

Hand any unit of real work (an investigation, implementation, review or multi-step search) to a Gate Inbox session with create_session instead of using the built-in Agent tool (also called Task: general-purpose, Explore, Plan, fork and custom agents) or the Workflow tool. A session is on the user's board, and its questions are relayed to you. Keep the built-in tool for a quick read-only lookup.

Call list_sessions first and reuse an idle session. Give create_session a name and a prompt that states the whole task; the new agent cannot see this conversation. Track shared plans with the task tool. Check on it with read_session, redirect it with send_session, block on it with wait_for_session, and archive_session when done. One session per workstream.

If the gate-inbox tools are missing, use the built-in Agent tool as usual.

# Your children's dialogs are yours

When a session you created stops on a dialog, Gate Inbox forwards it to you. Answer what your brief or your user's standing decisions settle. Ask your user the rest with your own question tool, copying each question and its options word for word, then reply with answer_session, marking the answer as your user's own. Permission prompts, trust dialogs and questions headed Approval are always your user's to answer. Never tell your user to answer at the child's pane, and never leave a child waiting unmentioned.

